  "Question": "The ratio of the measures of two acute angles is \\(5:4,\\) and the complement of one of these two angles is twice as large as the complement of the other. What is the sum of the degree measures of the two angles?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 75 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 90 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 135 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 150 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 270 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Represent the larger and smaller angle measures, in degrees, by \\(5t\\) and \\(4t\\). Because both angles are acute, \\(0<t<18\\). Their complements are \\(90-5t\\) and \\(90-4t\\).\n\nThe smaller angle has the larger complement, so the doubling condition must be\n\\[\n90-4t=2(90-5t).\n\\]\nExpanding and collecting terms gives\n\\[\n90-4t=180-10t,\n\\qquad 6t=90,\n\\qquad t=15.\n\\]\nThe angles are \\(75^\\circ\\) and \\(60^\\circ\\), both acute, and their complements are \\(15^\\circ\\) and \\(30^\\circ\\), as required. Their sum is \\(135^\\circ\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
